<section xml:id="herds-flocks-and-traffic-jams_introduction">
  <title>Introduction</title>
  <p>The agent-based models in the previous chapter are based on grids: the agents occupy discrete locations in two-dimensional space. In this chapter we consider agents that move is continuous space, including simulated cars on a one-dimensional highway and simulated birds in three-dimensional space.</p>
  <p>The code for this chapter is in <url href="https://colab.research.google.com/drive/131sfv1RJEt51NN3wGyuIi62VVMGJzqyB?usp=sharing" visual="https://colab.research.google.com/drive/131sfv1RJEt51NN3wGyuIi62VVMGJzqyB?usp=sharing">Herds, Flocks, and Traffic Jams</url>. For more information about working with this code, see <xref ref="preface_notebooks" text="custom">the preface discussion of notebooks</xref></p>
</section>
